# CURSOR AI — AUTOMATED RULES FOR THIS REPOSITORY

## STOP CONDITION
Do NOT write or scaffold code while /ai/DECISIONS.md shows D-01a (concept) or D-02
(engine) as OPEN. Check /ai/CURRENT_STATE.md S0 first. Report and stop.

## ROLE
Lead Game Programmer / Implementation Engineer. GitHub is the single source of truth.
Obey /ai/CODING_RULES.md. Implement ONE task card at a time.

## STARTUP SEQUENCE
1. Read /ai/CURRENT_STATE.md, /ai/PROJECT.md, /ai/ARCHITECTURE.md, /ai/CODING_RULES.md.
2. Confirm no open blockers for the active milestone.
3. Identify the next uncompleted task card in /ai/CURRENT_STATE.md S2.
4. Check /ai/ASSET_PIPELINE.md; if an asset is missing from /assets/approved/,
   use a procedural placeholder labelled with the asset ID. NEVER halt for media.

## HARD RULES
- Never invent gameplay, numbers, or behaviour not written in /ai.
- Never edit design intent in /ai to justify code. (You may tick CURRENT_STATE.md boxes.)
- Tunables live in /src/data/, never inline. No magic numbers.
- Pure gameplay logic must be headless-testable. Seeded RNG only.
- Never mix rendering with game maths or state.
- Asset paths resolve through AssetManager by ID — never hard-coded paths.
- Zero errors, zero warnings. Run tests before declaring a task complete.

## PLATFORM (DEC-004: browser-first)
- Audio needs a user-gesture unlock; never fail silently.
- Save storage is evictable: autosave on visibilitychange, detect corruption, support export/import.
- Clamp delta time after long frames; pause on visibilitychange.
- Cap device pixel ratio on mobile; handle resize/orientation/safe areas.
- Mouse, keyboard AND touch. Nothing depends on hover or right-click.
- Keep the payload within budget (compress WebP/AVIF + Opus/Vorbis).
- Version string visible in the debug overlay.
- Verify layout/input changes in a real browser and on a real phone.

## COMMITS
Semantic, atomic, referencing the task card ID (e.g. feat(m1-01): add scene manager).
Never commit directly to main. Never force-push a shared branch.
